course: dictionary
lesson: 14329
title: Words that are out of date
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Obsolete means no longer used, because something newer or better has taken its place. You can think of it as "out of date". Look at the words around it to check. «The floppy disk is obsolete, so most new computers do not have a slot for it.» The words newer and no slot are clues that the disk is old and no longer used.
explain: Obsolete is often used about machines and methods. «Typewriters became obsolete when computers arrived.» Computers were newer and better, so people stopped using typewriters. You can also say something «becomes obsolete» or that a newer thing «makes something obsolete».
explain: The word can also describe rules, laws and words. «That old rule is obsolete, so nobody follows it any more.» In biology, an obsolete body part has become very small or no longer works. To check your meaning, swap "out of date" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: Obsolete means no longer used because something newer or better has replaced it.
fact: «Obsolete technology» means machines and tools that are out of date, such as floppy disks, typewriters and fax machines.
fact: You can say «become obsolete» when something stops being used, and «make something obsolete» when a new thing replaces it.
fact: An obsolete rule or law is out of date and is not used any more.
fact: In biology, an obsolete body part has become very small or no longer works.
fact: Obsolete does not mean broken. A machine can still work and still be obsolete if something newer has replaced it.
exercise: «The typewriter is obsolete now that we have computers.» What does obsolete mean? | *No longer used, because something newer has replaced it | Brand new and shiny | Very expensive and rare | Heavy and hard to lift
exercise: Copy the one word that means out of date: «Floppy disks are obsolete, and most computers no longer have a slot for them.» | computers | disks | *obsolete | slot
exercise: Why might a company make a product obsolete? | *Because a newer, better product has replaced it | Because everyone loves it more every year | Because it is too cheap to sell | Because it has just been invented
exercise: Which words in «become obsolete» tell you what happens to the thing? | obsolete, meaning it is brand new | *become obsolete, meaning it stops being used | become, meaning it gets bigger | it is the only clue, and it means very loud
test: «Many schools have stopped using chalkboards, which are now obsolete.» What is the best meaning here? | Clean and easy to carry | Very expensive and hard to find | *Out of date and not used any more | Newly made and popular
test: Mia says, «The obsolete rule is the one everyone follows every day.» What is wrong with her idea? | Obsolete means very loud | *Obsolete means no longer used, so people do not follow it | Obsolete means very popular | Obsolete means brand new, so everyone follows it
exam: «The fax machine is obsolete.» Which phrase means the same as obsolete here? | very popular | very heavy | brand new | *out of date
